["<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>Perkins et al. v. Matthews, Mayor of the City of Canton, et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/5b7ebe24-f97e-4c4f-b583-b5b87f830e6d.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1792/2095\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>White, J.\nSome doubt about\nchange in polling\nplace than other\ntwo. On remedy,\nwouldn&#x27;t order another\nelection requiring\nelection which violates\nstate law — Courts remedy\nnot good one in above,\n&amp; if AG or 3 judge court\nfound polling places\nnon-discrim would\nlet election stand</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>Perkins et al. v. Matthews, Mayor of the City of Canton, et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/b42f1606-7a62-4d5e-b4c2-52171c2c425b.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:603/320\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Marshall, J.\nRevd</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>California v. Byers</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/49f2e3ac-a431-451f-ac08-d7eac45f346b.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1614/1211\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice Cal Sup Ct put places\nwrong. In 20th Cent we will be a\ndead end if we cant get drivers\nto stop &amp; give his name &amp; use it\nto prosecute him. Whether\ndoing so is a condition to drivers\nlicense, is just not testimonial\nwithin the Fifth amend-\nment, state can exact it.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>California v. Byers</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/2ac22d6b-7cf9-44a4-aa77-c1b49ad297dc.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1568/777\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Douglas, J. Never thought of law like\nthis in the criminal context\n- just that its part of valid\nregulation not gathered\nto make a criminal case</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>California v. Byers</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/2abefe93-2edb-4cb0-8bff-266becb77e2f.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1772/1801\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Harlan, J. This is an extension\nof Marchetti &amp; Grosso. The\nStates broad interests entitle\nthem to have laws that\nrequire a driver to\nincriminate himself. I&#x27;d\nface up to it &amp; say so,\nThis is not a cohale class\nof [underlined: gamblers] — the analogy\ncan be made to fit it but\nI wont go that far</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>California v. Byers</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/9af6daa6-d553-4eaf-85d4-4c91376f9f42.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1758/789\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Black, J. To compel man by law\nto give evidence against\nhimself - would go beyond\n&amp; say statute wholly\nvalid under Fifth amend</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>Amalgamated Association of Street, Electric Railway &amp; Motor Coach Employees of America et al. v. Lockridge</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/1281b767-4d77-4af7-9cd4-8e675efe5df5.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1580/1760\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice Some problems me\nWrongful termination of union membership\ntheory relied on by state court to\ntake it outside preemption. Thinks\nthere ought be room for some\ndoctrines of equity — here equit-\ndoctrine against forfeiture\nhas a role. He can&#x27;t be\nthrown out without something\nlike equity of redemption. Here\nhe was only 24-48 hours delin-\nquent</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>Amalgamated Association of Street, Electric Railway &amp; Motor Coach Employees of America et al. v. Lockridge</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/cf0472a3-b592-4c43-811b-3df41843509b.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1773/1278\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Black, J. dont think there should\nbe a forfeiture re 24-48 hour\ndelinquency. But who is to hear\nthe claim? He could have attacked\nhis [inserted: expulsion] [struck: suspension], but wrote a suit\nfor damages. So under\nBorden v Perko he had to go to\nNLRB</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>Amalgamated Association of Street, Electric Railway &amp; Motor Coach Employees of America et al. v. Lockridge</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/f8657d89-deaf-4338-ba8f-b9c183e467a2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1657/653\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Douglas, J. If he wanted reinstatement\nought go to NLRB. But if content\nto take damages, can sue</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>Amalgamated Association of Street, Electric Railway &amp; Motor Coach Employees of America et al. v. Lockridge</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/891dcda5-2dd2-4745-b0d9-37ab26cdd6ee.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1715/874\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Harlan, J.\nWould use this case to\noverrule Gonzales &amp; take\nGarmon as written in its\nfull sweep</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>Amalgamated Association of Street, Electric Railway &amp; Motor Coach Employees of America et al. v. Lockridge</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/54fe2cfe-c0d6-4c53-b76f-7c7c56eea16d.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1685/1644\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>White, J.\nThink Garmon doctrine is\njust overbroad (1) in\narea where employee can&#x27;t\nget an NLRB remedy\n(2) and where, as in case\nof this chap&#x27;s coll agree, the\nGeneral Counsel turns you\ndown when have a\ngood contract claim</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by William J. Brennan Jr</p><h2>United States v. Weller</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/c94b9e20-a54f-4f5f-bc34-35c1c8c6e2a2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1509/1094\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nWe have juris, Regulation has\nsupport in the statute. Congress\nrefused to authorize counsel\nwhen statute was proposed.\nIf Goldberg v Kelly controls\nthen I&#x27;d follow it. But\nwould certify to Court of\nappeals</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Donaldson, Fka Sweet v. United States et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/4955206b-d2ef-47c6-bcea-6d197467a1fc.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nCan&#x27;t agree with app&#x27;ting &quot;tie breaker.&quot;\n[struck: ID] No [inserted: need to] write an opinion.\nDeny N.M. motion to dismiss\nHave Master reconsider the &quot;double\nmass analysis.&quot;\n\nJustice Brennan\n[struck: It] &quot;No&quot; as to tie-breaker.\nSpecial Master should redefine the\n&#x27;47 Condition + go ahead + decide issues\nNeed a new S/M.\n\nJustice White\nBreitstein is outraged by failure of\nlawyers to get together. [struck: Fe] He is very able.\n[struck: Process is moot]\nOn merits, we can&#x27;t app&#x27;t a tie breaker.\nNor do [underlined: we] have auth. to decide\nissues left to Comm.\nSustain whatever Exceptions are\n[struck: nec] necessary to return case to S/M.\nMust rely on Experts — this is\nan arbitrary choice</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Donaldson, Fka Sweet v. United States et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/daa4e1cc-822e-4ca8-b116-1a12305d1320.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Justice Marshall\nAgree with BRW\n\nJustice Blackmun\nAgree generally with [struck: B]BRW\n\nJustice Powell\nSee my notes on p 2 of Report.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Donaldson, Fka Sweet v. United States et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/4786fd7e-1a3f-49ca-9173-9a8734bb67f3.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Justice Rehnquist\n[struck: Stev]\nNo Tiebreaker\nAgree with S/M as to double mass\n\nJustice Stevens\nS/M Report is not helpful. Should\nget a new S/M – a lawyer &amp; States will\npay for it.\n\nJustice O&#x27;Connor\nMaster should complete resolution of\nbasic data. Can quantify water\nby reliance on basic datas.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1971 term</p><h2>United States v. Campos-Serrano</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/971e7cfa-4d0c-4858-a572-1c8a196d8c07.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice Allen is directly in\npoint. changing places o polling\nplaces seems bad. But changing\nfrom ward to at large seems\ndifferent\n\nHarlan, J. Change of boundary\n[struck: not] precisely covered by\nAllen &amp; would affirm\nBut as to wards &amp;\nchanges of polling places\nthink they are little or\ndevices.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1971 term</p><h2>United States v. Campos-Serrano</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/b93d371f-89ae-4397-8ff5-31d09c2693d2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J. all three are these\ndevices DC had no\npower under statute to\ndetermine whether\nthese devices had\npurpose &amp; effect of\ndiscrim. Second to\nAG or 3 judge court\nfor that. Would not\nenter conditional\ninjunction\n\nWhite, J.\nMore doubt about\nchange in polling\nplace than other\ntwo. On remedy,\nwouldnt order another\nelection requiring\nelection which violates\nstate law. Courts remedy\nnot good one in action,\n&amp; if AG or 3 judge court\nfound polling places\nnon-discrim would\nlet election stand\n\nMarshall, J.\nWould</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1971 term</p><h2>Moose Lodge No. 107 v. Irvis et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/eb51a06a-bbd0-4e13-93c4-3158c1151218.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice Cal Sup Ct just plain\nwrong. In 20th Cent we will be a\ndead end if we can&#x27;t get driver\nto stop &amp; give his name &amp; use it\nto prosecute him. Whether\ndoing so is a condition to driver&#x27;s\nlicense, or just not testimonial\nwithin the Fifth Amend-\nment, state can exact it.\n\nBlack, J.\nTo compel man by law\nto give evidence against\nhimself — would go beyond\n&amp; say statute wholly\nvalid under Fifth Amend\n\nDouglas, J. Never thought of law like\nthis in the criminal context\n— just that its part of whole\nregulation. Not gathered\nto make a criminal case\n\nHarlan, J. This is an extension\nof Marchetti &amp; Grosso. The\nstates broad interests entitle\nthem to have laws that\nrequire a driver to\nincriminate himself. Sd\nface up to it &amp; say so.\nThis is not a select class\nof gamblers — the analogy\ncan be made to fit it but\nI won&#x27;t go that far</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1971 term</p><h2>North Carolina v. Rice</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/26ac5d1c-3989-4780-af6f-36bc2d182df2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nWe have juris, Regulation has\nsupport in the statute. Congress\nrefused to authorize counsel\nwhen statute was proposed.\nIf Goldberg v Kelly controls\nthen I&#x27;d follow it. But\nwould certify to Court of\nappeals</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1971 term</p><h2>D. H. Overmyer Co., Inc., of Ohio et al. v. Frick Co.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/b98f499f-01bd-4278-9658-072dbd2734bf.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2250\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre><span class=\"wait\">No writing on this page.</span></pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1971 term</p><h2>Wisconsin v. Yoder et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/66a00252-9148-4281-855a-7de6a8ce388a.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2250\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre><span class=\"wait\">No writing on this page.</span></pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1971 term</p><h2>Groppi v. Leslie, Sheriff</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><bu